  - Native SLM validation checks header bounds, nonzero checksum match, byte-tokenizer metadata, duplicate tensor hashes, required tensor names and shapes, dtype-specific byte lengths, finite f32 payload values, and quantization scale ranges.
  - Seven current local .slm artifacts pass native validation: tiny f32/q8/q4/BPE and TinyLM-16M-shaped f32/q8/q4.
  - Seven current local .slm artifacts have .slm.manifest provenance sidecars validated by tinyrustlm-slm-pack validate-manifest.
